# Reads across a table's growth while simplify writes a module: with 496 constants ahead the
# dot writer's operands (an operand's instruction grows the id table before the next name is
# read), with 1100 the cost of a variable (its name is a symbol, not a node: read as one past
# the node table, which only an ASan build sees).

simplify nofile
```spv
OpCapability Shader
OpMemoryModel Logical GLSL450
OpEntryPoint Fragment %main "main" %in %out
OpExecutionMode %main OriginUpperLeft
OpDecorate %in Flat
OpDecorate %in Location 0
OpDecorate %out Location 0
%void = OpTypeVoid
%fn = OpTypeFunction %void
%uint = OpTypeInt 32 0
